WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:04.957
Here is the learning path for this module We begin
with the

00:00:04.983 --> 00:00:10.551
core aggregate functions COUNT SUM AVG MIN and MAX
Then

00:00:10.578 --> 00:00:13.841
we use GROUP BY to create one summary row for each
category

00:00:13.854 --> 00:00:19.755
or combination of categories After that we separate
WHERE from HAVING

00:00:20.692 --> 00:00:25.731
WHERE decides which source rows are allowed into the
aggregation HAVING decides

00:00:25.745 --> 00:00:30.933
which completed groups stay in the final result We
then extend the

00:00:30.946 --> 00:00:36.564
same ideas with conditional aggregation PostgreSQL
FILTER ROLLUP CUBE GROUPING SETS

00:00:36.762 --> 00:00:43.057
and window functions The practice pattern also
becomes gradually more independent

00:00:43.981 --> 00:00:47.744
First you run complete examples then change them
then fill in missing

00:00:47.757 --> 00:00:51.191
pieces and finally write short analytical queries
yourself
